WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.599
Rose had trouble sleeping that night.

2
00:00:15.659 --> 00:00:18.520
She was eager to learn more about the mystery of Oliver's family.

3
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.802
But Nancy had come to her in confidence and trusted her with the information that Monks and Oliver

4
00:00:23.842 --> 00:00:24.382
were brothers.

5
00:00:25.482 --> 00:00:30.343
Nancy's manner had touched Rose's heart, and Rose hoped that somehow she could help the miserable young woman.

6
00:00:31.324 --> 00:00:34.545
But Rose also loved Oliver, and there wasn't much time to help him.

7
00:00:35.646 --> 00:00:39.368
Mrs. Maylie, Oliver, and Rose were going to be in London for only two more days.

8
00:00:40.509 --> 00:00:42.730
Then they would be traveling to the coast for several weeks.

9
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:46.852
"I have to make a plan that can be executed in 48 hours!"

10
00:00:47.233 --> 00:00:48.093
Rose told herself.

11
00:00:49.214 --> 00:00:50.695
She sat up in bed, wide awake.

12
00:00:50.715 --> 00:00:54.677
"Or perhaps I can postpone our journey without causing suspicion!"

13
00:00:56.418 --> 00:00:59.020
Dr. Losberne was also staying with them at the London hotel.

14
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.401
But Rose was well acquainted with the excellent gentleman's impetuosity.

15
00:01:04.441 --> 00:01:08.922
If he learned that Nancy was the one who had captured Oliver for Fagin, he'd scour the city

16
00:01:08.962 --> 00:01:09.803
until he found her.

17
00:01:09.823 --> 00:01:12.543
"Then who knows what rash act Dr.

18
00:01:12.563 --> 00:01:14.364
Losberne might commit," Rose murmured.

19
00:01:15.484 --> 00:01:16.685
"No, I can't tell him.

20
00:01:17.805 --> 00:01:21.386
I also can't confide in my aunt because the first thing she'll do is consult Dr.

21
00:01:21.406 --> 00:01:24.267
Losberne. Maybe I could write to Harry."

22
00:01:25.287 --> 00:01:29.288
But then she remembered the last time she'd seen Harry, when she'd refused his marriage proposal.

23
00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:31.541
Tears came to her eyes.

24
00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:36.503
Still uncertain what to do, Rose lay down and finally fell asleep.

25
00:01:37.624 --> 00:01:40.445
The next morning she reluctantly decided to consult Harry.

26
00:01:41.506 --> 00:01:45.068
She sat with pen and paper, trying to write, but she couldn't think of what to say.

27
00:01:46.168 --> 00:01:48.090
Just then Oliver burst into her room.

28
00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:50.591
He had been out walking with Mr.

29
00:01:50.611 --> 00:01:52.312
Giles, and his face was flushed.

30
00:01:52.332 --> 00:01:54.693
"What's wrong?"

31
00:01:55.113 --> 00:01:56.014
asked Rose in alarm.

32
00:01:56.034 --> 00:01:59.916
"I hardly know where to begin," Oliver said breathlessly.

33
00:02:01.064 --> 00:02:01.845
"I've seen him!

34
00:02:03.006 --> 00:02:05.008
At last you'll know that I was telling you the truth."

35
00:02:06.189 --> 00:02:07.270
"Who are you talking about?"

36
00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:08.230
asked Rose.

37
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.773
"The gentleman who was so good to me.

38
00:02:10.813 --> 00:02:11.693
Mr. Brownlow."

39
00:02:11.713 --> 00:02:13.775
"Where did you see him?"

40
00:02:14.916 --> 00:02:17.438
Rose laid down her pen, all thoughts of her letter forgotten.

41
00:02:17.458 --> 00:02:20.441
"Getting out of a coach and going into a house.

42
00:02:21.582 --> 00:02:23.744
I was trembling so much that I couldn't speak to him.

43
00:02:24.745 --> 00:02:25.165
But Mr.

44
00:02:25.205 --> 00:02:26.786
Giles asked a servant whether Mr.

45
00:02:26.826 --> 00:02:28.428
Brownlow lives there and he does!"

46
00:02:29.564 --> 00:02:31.285
Oliver showed Rose a scrap of paper.

47
00:02:31.305 --> 00:02:33.145
"Here's his address.

48
00:02:34.285 --> 00:02:34.986
Oh, dear me!

49
00:02:36.006 --> 00:02:37.446
What shall I do when I see him?"

50
00:02:37.466 --> 00:02:40.427
"Quick!" said Rose.

51
00:02:40.447 --> 00:02:44.528
"Find someone to fetch us a coach and be ready to go with me in a few minutes.

52
00:02:45.668 --> 00:02:48.349
I'll tell my aunt that we're going out, but I won't say anything more.

53
00:02:49.409 --> 00:02:49.929
Now hurry!"

54
00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.250
In just over five minutes, they were on their way to Mr.

55
00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.011
Brownlow's house.

56
00:02:55.111 --> 00:02:58.012
Rose left Oliver in the coach under the pretense of preparing Mr.

57
00:02:58.052 --> 00:02:59.092
Brownlow for his arrival.

58
00:03:00.188 --> 00:03:02.409
A servant led her upstairs to a room, where Mr.

59
00:03:02.429 --> 00:03:03.290
Brownlow was sitting.

60
00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:07.992
"I have some news that will no doubt surprise you," said Rose after Mr.

61
00:03:08.012 --> 00:03:09.553
Brownlow had invited her to sit.

62
00:03:09.573 --> 00:03:12.894
"You once took an interest in a young friend of mine."

63
00:03:13.935 --> 00:03:15.075
"Indeed, who is that?"

64
00:03:15.456 --> 00:03:16.636
Mr. Brownlow was intrigued.

65
00:03:16.656 --> 00:03:18.557
"Oliver Twist."

66
00:03:19.558 --> 00:03:21.839
Mr. Brownlow was astonished to hear that name again.

67
00:03:21.859 --> 00:03:23.880
"What has become of him?"

68
00:03:25.576 --> 00:03:26.337
Rose told Mr.

69
00:03:26.377 --> 00:03:30.660
Brownlow everything that had happened to Oliver since that fateful day when he left for the bookseller's.

70
00:03:31.681 --> 00:03:33.643
But she did not share what Nancy had told her.

71
00:03:33.663 --> 00:03:36.625
"I'm very happy to hear this news of Oliver.

72
00:03:37.746 --> 00:03:38.347
Very happy.

73
00:03:39.348 --> 00:03:40.889
But you haven't told me where he is now."

74
00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:43.531
"He's waiting in a coach at the door."

75
00:03:43.551 --> 00:03:45.293
"At my door?"

76
00:03:45.593 --> 00:03:46.514
cried the old gentleman.

77
00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:50.917
With that he hurried from the room, down the stairs, and into the coach.

78
00:03:52.138 --> 00:03:53.559
"Oliver!" exclaimed Mr.

79
00:03:53.579 --> 00:03:56.185
Brownlow. "I knew you'd come back!"

80
00:03:57.245 --> 00:04:02.207
Overcome by tears of happiness, Oliver could not speak, but he embraced Mr.

81
00:04:02.247 --> 00:04:06.249
Brownlow. Hand in hand, they returned to the room where Rose was waiting.

82
00:04:06.269 --> 00:04:09.150
"There's someone else whom we should not forget."

83
00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.771
Mr. Brownlow rang the bell, summoning his housekeeper.

84
00:04:14.532 --> 00:04:16.393
Mrs. Bedwin responded to the bell at once.

85
00:04:17.593 --> 00:04:18.713
Dropping a curtsy to Mr.

86
00:04:18.753 --> 00:04:20.354
Brownlow, she waited for his orders.

87
00:04:20.374 --> 00:04:22.915
"Can't you see why I've summoned you?"

88
00:04:23.215 --> 00:04:24.776
Mr. Brownlow said somewhat crossly.

89
00:04:25.804 --> 00:04:26.705
"Put on your glasses."

90
00:04:27.886 --> 00:04:29.567
The old lady rummaged in her pocket.

91
00:04:30.628 --> 00:04:32.790
But Oliver could not wait for her to find her glasses.

92
00:04:34.011 --> 00:04:35.872
He ran to her and sprang into her arms.

93
00:04:35.892 --> 00:04:38.435
"My innocent boy!"

94
00:04:38.815 --> 00:04:40.076
she exclaimed as she hugged him.

95
00:04:40.096 --> 00:04:42.318
"My dear nurse!"

96
00:04:42.698 --> 00:04:43.339
cried Oliver.

97
00:04:43.359 --> 00:04:45.660
"I knew you would come back.

98
00:04:46.761 --> 00:04:47.722
How well you look!

99
00:04:48.823 --> 00:04:51.165
The same sweet face, but not so pale.

100
00:04:52.246 --> 00:04:54.528
The same gentle eyes, but not so sad.

101
00:04:55.688 --> 00:04:56.689
Where have you been?"

102
00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.511
Oliver began to tell his story.

103
00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:02.993
"I must speak to you alone," Rose whispered to Mr.

104
00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:08.137
Brownlow. He led her into another room, where she revealed to him what Nancy had told her.

105
00:05:09.898 --> 00:05:12.800
Rose also explained why she could not tell her aunt or Dr.

106
00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:16.023
Losberne. "A wise decision," said Mr.

107
00:05:16.043 --> 00:05:17.924
Brownlow. "Leave Dr.

108
00:05:17.944 --> 00:05:18.645
Losberne to me.

109
00:05:19.745 --> 00:05:23.048
I will call at the hotel this evening at eight o'clock and explain everything to him."

110
00:05:24.136 --> 00:05:28.537
Rose and Oliver soon had to return to the hotel, with Oliver promising to visit Mrs.

111
00:05:28.577 --> 00:05:29.197
Bedwin again.

112
00:05:30.258 --> 00:05:30.998
That night Mr.

113
00:05:31.018 --> 00:05:31.978
Brownlow met with Dr.

114
00:05:32.018 --> 00:05:32.838
Losberne, Mrs.

115
00:05:32.878 --> 00:05:33.739
Maylie, and Rose.

116
00:05:34.939 --> 00:05:38.040
Oliver was left alone in the next room, so he wouldn't hear what was said.

117
00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.821
Dr. Losberne was every bit as angry as Rose had feared.

118
00:05:42.921 --> 00:05:46.862
As soon as he heard Nancy's story, he was halfway out the door, threatening to track her down.

119
00:05:48.082 --> 00:05:48.683
Somehow Mr.

120
00:05:48.703 --> 00:05:51.083
Brownlow managed to stop him from going to the police.

121
00:05:52.284 --> 00:05:53.664
"So what are we supposed to do now?"

122
00:05:53.996 --> 00:05:55.437
Dr. Losberne said impatiently.

123
00:05:55.457 --> 00:06:01.343
"We need to find out who Oliver's parents were and discover if Nancy's story is true," said Mr.

124
00:06:01.363 --> 00:06:06.007
Brownlow. "Is this man Monks really trying to cheat Oliver out of his inheritance?

125
00:06:07.128 --> 00:06:10.491
First we must ask Nancy if she's willing to point out Monks to us so we can deal

126
00:06:10.531 --> 00:06:10.831
with him."

127
00:06:11.912 --> 00:06:15.375
"That means we can't meet her until Sunday night—five days away," said Dr.

128
00:06:15.395 --> 00:06:19.899
Losberne. "But that will give me time to contact Harry Maylie, who will be a great help to

129
00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:20.520
us, I'm sure.

130
00:06:21.652 --> 00:06:22.132
He's Mrs.

131
00:06:22.172 --> 00:06:24.093
Maylie's son and a dear friend of Rose's."

132
00:06:25.254 --> 00:06:27.154
Rose blushed deeply but didn't say anything.

133
00:06:27.174 --> 00:06:30.796
"We will remain in London, of course," said Mrs.

134
00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:33.757
Maylie. "I don't care how long this takes."

135
00:06:34.898 --> 00:06:35.918
Mr. Brownlow stood up.

136
00:06:36.979 --> 00:06:37.919
"Now let's go to supper.

137
00:06:38.959 --> 00:06:42.441
Poor Oliver probably thinks we've tired of him and are plotting how to get rid of him."
